# Reinsurance adjudicator — canonical data types

> Module Schema

Amounts are integers in the contract's minor unit (cents), matching the `Nat`
arithmetic of `ReinsuranceLean`. Dates are day numbers since 1970-01-01, so every
comparison is an exact integer comparison and no calendar library is involved.

Perils and clause identifiers are **enumerations**, not free text: a verdict cites
a typed clause, so a citation cannot drift into prose and cannot be misspelled.

```catala
declaration enumeration VerdictKind:
  -- Covered
  -- Reserved
  -- Excluded
  -- Incomplete

declaration enumeration Peril:
  -- Windstorm
  -- Flood
  -- Earthquake
  -- Fire
  -- Cyber
  -- War

declaration enumeration Clause:
  -- Cl_4_1_PerilsInsured
  -- Cl_4_2_PerilExclusion
  -- Cl_5_1_CyberExclusion
  -- Cl_5_1a_CyberResultingFireWriteBack
  -- Cl_5_2_WarExclusion
  -- Cl_6_1_TreatyPeriod
  -- Cl_7_3_Certification
  -- Cl_7_4_UnresolvedCourtRulingReserve
  -- Cl_8_1_LimitAndRetention

declaration enumeration PendingKind:
  -- OccurrenceAggregation
  -- LegalInterpretation
  -- AdjusterCertification

declaration structure Claim:
  # The claim reference is carried outside Catala: the language has no string
  # type in 1.2, and the reference is not part of the coverage decision.
  data lossAmount content integer
  data peril content Peril
  data incidentDay content integer
  data isCertified content boolean
  data litigationFinal content boolean
  data resultingFireOrExplosion content boolean

declaration structure TreatyTerms:
  data retention content integer
  data limit content integer
  data reinstatements content integer
  data reinstatementRateBps content integer
  data inceptionDay content integer
  data expiryDay content integer
  data excludesFlood content boolean
  data excludesEarthquake content boolean

declaration structure Verdict:
  data kind content VerdictKind
  data citedClauses content list of Clause
  data pending content list of PendingKind
```
